], [55, 790]]}, {"text": "Prime factorization of 24", "conf": 0.897, "box": [[53, 807], [315, 803], [316, 829], [54, 834]]}, {"text": "common prime factors of 18 and 24 = 2, 3", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[58, 849], [496, 844], [497, 872], [59, 876]]}, {"text": "product of 2 and. 3", "conf": 0.918, "box": [[51, 886], [242, 883], [243, 909], [52, 912]]}, {"text": "=2×3=6", "conf": 0.741, "box": [[376, 888], [496, 888], [496, 911], [376, 911]]}, {"text": "6 is the greatest factor which divides both 18 and 24 completely.", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[50, 921], [720, 922], [720, 955], [50, 954]]}, {"text": "6 is called the HCF of 18 and 24", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[52, 968], [385, 967], [385, 993], [52, 994]]}, {"text": "The greatest possible length of each piece is 6 cm.", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[53, 1008], [585, 1009], [585, 1037], [53, 1035]]}, {"text": "Key Fact", "conf": 0.833, "box": [[134, 1102], [238, 1104], [237, 1135], [133, 1133]]}, {"text": "The greatest number which divides 2 or more", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[65, 1153], [465, 1161], [465, 1185], [64, 1177]]}, {"text": "numbers simultaneously, is called their HCF.", "conf": 0.877, "box": [[62, 1177], [455, 1184], [455, 1211], [61, 1203]]}, {"text": "Give ropes of diferent lengths to the students.Ask them to divide the pieces of ropes", "conf": 0.889, "box": [[120, 1232], [824, 1241], [824, 1273], [120, 1265]]}, {"text": "in equal lengths.", "conf": 0.863, "box": [[124, 1262], [253, 1266], [253, 1290], [123, 1287]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.862, "box": [[47, 1331], [193, 1336], [192, 1360], [46, 1355]]}, {"text": "31", "conf": 0.664, "box": [[451, 1342], [485, 1342], [485, 1371], [451, 1371]]}, {"text": "downloaded from awazeinqilab.com", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[179, 1473], [749, 1473], [749, 1509], [179, 1509]]}]}